{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MT7Xp2qXfKbNiqUkg7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run test:ssr`, `npm test` and `npm run size` pass\n\nTicket 05 is finished and committed in four commits. Lint is clean, `npm run test:ssr` passes 80/80, `npm test` passes 290/290, and `npm run size` is within its limits.\n\nThe server now wraps non-empty component children in `<!--[c-->`…`<!--]-->` (in `src/htm.ts`). A component with no children gets no children markers. The exact-string checks for static pages pass unchanged.\n\nThe browser side is in `src/htm.browser.ts`:\n- **Finding the children:** `_range` now looks for the `[c` marker instead of the first region marker, so a region in a component's own render is no longer mistaken for its children.\n- **Matching the close:** `_close` treats any comment starting with `[` as an opener, so the depth count covers both kinds of marker.\n- **Created hosts:** `_createHost` emits the same marker, so hosts created in the browser are found the same way when they are morphed later.\n- `_skip` needed no change, because it already skips every comment except `[`.\n\nThe tests are in `test/ssr.ts` and `test/index.ts`:\n- **SSR:** the children assertion now expects the new marker, and a new check covers the no-children case.\n- **Region before children:** a new adoption test checks that a button inside the children of such a component fires its listener.\n- **Existing fixture:** the old children-range test now uses `<!--[c-->`.\n\nThe depth-matching test passed as soon as the browser change landed, so it never went red on its own. My first version could not catch a depth bug, because adoption carries on past a range end that comes too early. The final version re-runs a region around the host so the children range is morphed. With depth counting temporarily broken, it fails.\n\nThe browser templater measures 4.57 kB against its 4.6 kB limit, so I didn't raise it. `npm run size` measures `dist/`, so I rebuilt before measuring.\n\nI updated the **Reactive region** entry in `CONTEXT.md`, ADR-007 (the decision text plus a dated note) and the marker lines in `AGENTS.md`.\n\n`npm test` serves on port 8123, and the first final run failed because another worktree's test run was using that port. I left that process alone, waited for the port to free up and re-ran; the 290/290 result is from the re-run. Notes for the next attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":79346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439},"output_tokens":694,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e566ad36-7644-415a-8af3-f5e97c46f1bd","uuid":"4084e5cd-397a-4033-80ba-dbcd670e4116","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:59:23.186Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MT7GwNv6k3g2s69pgP"}
